    "why": "Owner decision K: a weekly-cadence duty's end is spanDays' business, so the backup week starting 1 August at 08:00 ends on the SEVENTH date, 7 August at 18:00 -- not the eighth, which the plan's original + spanDays formula would have given. The 10 h exclusion therefore runs to 8 August 04:00. The night starting 7 August at 17:00 is BEFORE the window opens and is clean; the dawn duty starting 8 August at 03:00 is inside it and is not. Owner decision H's start-in-window is what those two placements are measuring: the second duty is tested by where it STARTS, not by whether it overlaps.",
